#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Check on the switchboard and the orchestrators it watches. No LLM.

Usage: switchboard-health --once [--dry-run] [--state-dir DIR]
                          [--env KEY=VALUE ...] [--path DIR ...] [--login MARK]

Run every 5 minutes by switchboard-health-ctl: a launch agent on macOS, a
Task Scheduler task on Windows. One pass reads the switchboard's state file
(written only by switchboard-state): $SWITCHBOARD_STATE when it is set, else
DIR/state.md, as for switchboard-state and switchboard-wait. It reads
`herdr agent list` too, then checks in this order:

  1. The switchboard pane: the agent whose name is "switchboard", else whose
     title is (herdr's title, else its terminal title). Blocked (a prompt it
     cannot clear itself): banner to the user. Missing (pane gone or its
     agent exited): restart it, see below.
  2. Its cycle: state.md's last line is "CYCLE <date>" and the pane is idle:
     send "/clear", then, once herdr reports a new session id for the pane
     (the sign /clear took, waited for up to 30 s), "/rename switchboard"
     and "/switchboard resume". The fingerprint holds the CYCLE line's date.
     Still the last line, with the pane idle, on a later pass: send the
     three again, once. Still there on the pass after that: banner.
  3. The waits: `switchboard-wait --status` on every watched repo. "wait none"
     with the switchboard idle, on two passes in a row: prompt
     "SWITCHBOARD HEALTH wait-none: <repo>". Not counted while the CYCLE
     marker is there, because a switchboard asking to be cycled has stopped
     watching on purpose.
  4. The orchestrators. A pane blocked, or idle with no trailing CYCLE or
     DONE, on two passes in a row: prompt
     "SWITCHBOARD HEALTH check-in <project>: <condition>". A pane working
     whose .legwork/switchboard.md mtime and herdr state_change_seq have not
     moved for 60 minutes: prompt "SWITCHBOARD HEALTH stall <project>: <N>
     min with no change" and show a banner.

"Idle" means herdr's idle or done: both mean the agent is ready for input.
Prompts go only to an idle switchboard, never with Esc or any other key, so
a running wait is never cut short. At most one prompt lands per pass: once
one is sent the switchboard is busy with it, so the rest are logged as
deferred and sent on later passes, in check order. A prompt that has to
wait for an idle switchboard is deferred the same way.

Every alert has a fingerprint (repo, pane, condition). One fingerprint
prompts once and banners once, until a pass no longer sees the condition. A
banner is terminal-notifier on macOS (found on PATH, else in /opt/homebrew/bin)
and a Windows toast through powershell.exe on Windows. A banner that cannot be
shown writes a note to stderr and is logged as failed, and the fingerprint
stays open, so the next pass tries again.

Restart: when the switchboard is missing, open a workspace in the legwork
folder (LEGWORK_DIR, else this checkout) with DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATE=true,
LEGWORK_SWITCHBOARD_DIR=DIR, and the job's CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and
SWITCHBOARD_STATE when it has them (a scheduled job has no current pane to
split), so the new switchboard finds the same state file. Then name the
pane, `herdr agent start switchboard --kind claude ... --
<LEGWORK_SESSION_ARGS>` (default "--model opus --effort high"), then send
"/rename switchboard" and "/switchboard resume". The folder must be one Claude
Code already trusts, or the start stops at the trust question. At most one
restart an hour. Missing again inside that hour, or a start that ends in
agent_not_ready, shows a banner asking the user to start it by hand, and does
not retry until the hour is up. With no state.md the switchboard has never
run, so nothing is checked or restarted. A state.md that watches nothing is
not restarted either: the user may have closed the switchboard on purpose.
Both are logged as a note.

Switching itself off: a pass that finds nothing to watch (no state.md, or a
state.md that watches nothing and has no CYCLE marker), after a pass that
found the same, runs `switchboard-health-ctl off` as its last act, once the
pass is logged. The switchboard switches the watcher on when it starts and
off when its watch list empties; this catches the times it could not, such
as a /clear or a closed pane. The count starts again after a long gap and
after switching off, so a watcher switched on again gets two passes.

--login MARK (Windows): the sign-in the task was switched on in. A pass in a
later sign-in switches the watcher off and checks nothing, so on Windows too
the watcher is off after every sign-in until it is switched on again. A
macOS launch agent goes at logout by itself.

--env KEY=VALUE sets one environment variable for the pass, before any
setting is read. The Windows task uses it to carry CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and the
legwork settings, as the launch agent's environment does on macOS. --path DIR
puts DIR first on PATH for the pass; the Windows task uses it for the folder
herdr was found in when the watcher was switched on.

With no stdout or stderr (the Windows task runs under pythonw.exe), the pass
appends them to DIR/health.out.log and DIR/health.err.log, the files the
launch agent writes on macOS.

Each pass appends one JSON line to DIR/health.jsonl and keeps fingerprints,
two-pass counts, the off count, stall clocks, the last pass and the last
restart in DIR/health-state.json. A pass more than 15 minutes after the last
one (the computer slept, or the job did not run) restarts every stall clock
and two-pass count, so a sleep is never read as a stall. Prompts and banners
already sent stay sent. It never writes state.md.

A pane id that is not a plain id or name (not a string, empty, or starting
with "-") never reaches herdr: it is logged as an error and that check is
skipped. A check of one repo that fails for any reason is logged as an
error line, its alerts carried over, and the pass goes on to the next.

--dry-run prints what the pass would do, sends nothing, starts nothing and
writes nothing (not even the log), so it is safe against the real state.
--state-dir defaults to LEGWORK_SWITCHBOARD_DIR (environment or legwork
config), else $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/switchboard, else ~/.claude/switchboard:
the folder switchboard-state and switchboard-wait use when SWITCHBOARD_STATE
is not set. The watcher's own files always go in DIR.

Exit 0 after a pass, 2 on bad arguments.
"""
import base64
import html
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(1, os.path.join(HERE, ".."))
try:
    from settings import setting  # orchestration/settings.py, same checkout
except ImportError:  # copied out of the checkout: environment only
    def setting(key, default=None):
        return os.environ.get(key) or default

WINDOWS = os.name == "nt"
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(HERE))  # the legwork checkout this script is in
HOMEBREW_NOTIFIER = "/opt/homebrew/bin/terminal-notifier"
NOTIFIER = shutil.which("terminal-notifier") or (
    HOMEBREW_NOTIFIER if os.path.exists(HOMEBREW_NOTIFIER) else None)
POWERSHELL = shutil.which("powershell.exe") or (
    os.path.join(os.environ["SystemRoot"], "System32", "WindowsPowerShell", "v1.0",
                 "powershell.exe") if os.environ.get("SystemRoot") else None)
WAIT = os.path.join(HERE, "switchboard-wait")
CTL = os.path.join(HERE, "switchboard-health-ctl")
STATE_FILE = None  # $SWITCHBOARD_STATE, else DIR/state.md, set per pass
STATE_DIR = None  # DIR, set per pass
NAME = "switchboard"
TITLE = "legwork switchboard"
SESSION_ARGS = "--model opus --effort high"
READY = ("idle", "done")
CYCLE_PROMPTS = ("/clear", "/rename switchboard", "/switchboard resume")
RESUME_PROMPTS = ("/rename switchboard", "/switchboard resume")
HERDR_TIMEOUT = 30
CLEAR_TIMEOUT = 30  # seconds to wait for /clear to start a new session
CLEAR_POLL = 1
START_TIMEOUT = 90  # seconds herdr gives Claude Code to come up
STALL = 60 * 60
RESTART_GAP = 60 * 60
PASS_GAP = 15 * 60  # longer than this between passes: start counting again
OFF_PASSES = 2  # passes in a row with nothing to watch before switching off
BY_HAND = ("Start it yourself: run /switchboard resume in a Claude Code pane "
           "named switchboard.")
ENV_KEY = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*")

# The toast, shown by Windows PowerShell 5.1 through the WinRT types it can
# load with no module. The text comes in through the environment, never
# into the script. The app id is PowerShell's own, which Windows knows.
TOAST = r"""
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$ProgressPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'
$null = [Windows.UI.Notifications.ToastNotificationManager, Windows.UI.Notifications, ContentType = WindowsRuntime]
$null = [Windows.Data.Xml.Dom.XmlDocument, Windows.Data.Xml.Dom.XmlDocument, ContentType = WindowsRuntime]
$e = [System.Security.SecurityElement]
$xml = New-Object Windows.Data.Xml.Dom.XmlDocument
$xml.LoadXml('<toast><visual><binding template="ToastGeneric"><text>' + $e::Escape($env:LEGWORK_TOAST_TITLE) + '</text><text>' + $e::Escape($env:LEGWORK_TOAST_TEXT) + '</text></binding></visual></toast>')
$app = '{1AC14E77-02E7-4E5D-B744-2EB1AE5198B7}\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe'
[Windows.UI.Notifications.ToastNotificationManager]::CreateToastNotifier($app).Show([Windows.UI.Notifications.ToastNotification]::new($xml))
"""

PANE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9:_.-]*")


def now():
    return time.time()


def default_state_dir():
    return (setting("LEGWORK_SWITCHBOARD_DIR")
            or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR")
                                               or "~/.claude"), "switchboard"))


def legwork_dir():
    """The switchboard pane's start folder: LEGWORK_DIR, else this checkout."""
    return setting("LEGWORK_DIR") or ROOT


def session_args():
    """LEGWORK_SESSION_ARGS as a list. On Windows a backslash is a path
    separator, not an escape, so it is kept; quotes still group words."""
    value = setting("LEGWORK_SESSION_ARGS") or SESSION_ARGS
    if not WINDOWS:
        return shlex.split(value)
    args = []
    for word in shlex.split(value, posix=False):
        if len(word) >= 2 and word[0] == word[-1] and word[0] in "\"'":
            word = word[1:-1]
        args.append(word)
    return args


def state_file(state_dir):
    """The switchboard's state file: $SWITCHBOARD_STATE, else DIR/state.md."""
    named = os.environ.get("SWITCHBOARD_STATE")
    return os.path.expanduser(named) if named else os.path.join(state_dir, "state.md")


def plain_error(text):
    """powershell.exe's stderr in plain words. Windows PowerShell 5.1 writes
    it as CLIXML when stderr is not a console, often with a progress record
    first, so only its error strings are kept."""
    if not text.lstrip().startswith("#< CLIXML"):
        return text
    parts = re.findall(r'<S S="Error">(.*?)</S>', text, re.S)
    words = re.sub(r"_x([0-9A-Fa-f]{4})_", lambda m: chr(int(m.group(1), 16)), "".join(parts))
    return " ".join(html.unescape(words).split())


def log_to_files(state_dir):
    """Under pythonw.exe there is no stdout or stderr: append them to DIR's
    log files, as the launch agent does on macOS."""
    for stream, name in (("stdout", "health.out.log"), ("stderr", "health.err.log")):
        if getattr(sys, stream) is not None:
            continue
        try:
            os.makedirs(state_dir, exist_ok=True)
            setattr(sys, stream, open(os.path.join(state_dir, name), "a", buffering=1,
                                      encoding="utf-8", errors="replace", newline="\n"))
        except OSError:
            pass


def call(argv, timeout, env=None):
    """Run one command and return its CompletedProcess, output as text. On
    Windows no console window opens for it. The tests replace this."""
    extra = {}
    if os.name == "nt":
        extra["creationflags"] = getattr(subprocess, "CREATE_NO_WINDOW", 0)
    return subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace",
                          timeout=timeout, env=env, **extra)


def child_python():
    """The interpreter for the scripts this pass runs. The Windows task runs
    under pythonw.exe; its console twin keeps their own herdr calls from
    opening a window."""
    exe = sys.executable
    if os.path.basename(exe).lower() == "pythonw.exe":
        twin = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(exe), "python.exe")
        if os.path.exists(twin):
            return twin
    return exe


def login_mark():
    """This Windows sign-in's logon time, as a string, or None when it cannot
    be read (or off Windows). An RDP reconnect keeps it; a new sign-in or a
    reboot changes it."""
    if os.name != "nt":
        return None
    try:
        import ctypes
        from ctypes import wintypes

        class Info(ctypes.Structure):  # WTSINFOW
            _fields_ = ([("State", ctypes.c_int), ("SessionId", wintypes.DWORD)]
                        + [(n, wintypes.DWORD) for n in (
                            "InBytes", "OutBytes", "InFrames", "OutFrames",
                            "InCompressed", "OutCompressed")]
                        + [("Station", ctypes.c_wchar * 32), ("Domain", ctypes.c_wchar * 17),
                           ("User", ctypes.c_wchar * 21)]
                        + [(n, ctypes.c_longlong) for n in (
                            "ConnectTime", "DisconnectTime", "LastInputTime", "LogonTime",
                            "CurrentTime")])

        wts = ctypes.WinDLL("wtsapi32")
        buf, size = ctypes.c_void_p(), wintypes.DWORD()
        # WTS_CURRENT_SESSION, WTSSessionInfo
        if not wts.WTSQuerySessionInformationW(None, wintypes.DWORD(0xFFFFFFFF), 24,
                                               ctypes.byref(buf), ctypes.byref(size)):
            return None
        try:
            if size.value < ctypes.sizeof(Info):
                return None
            logon = ctypes.cast(buf, ctypes.POINTER(Info)).contents.LogonTime
        finally:
            wts.WTSFreeMemory(buf)
        return str(logon) if logon > 0 else None
    except (OSError, AttributeError, ValueError):
        return None


def valid_pane(pane):
    """True for a pane id or agent name herdr can take as one argument, never a flag."""
    return isinstance(pane, str) and PANE.fullmatch(pane) is not None


def herdr(*args, timeout=HERDR_TIMEOUT):
    """(result, None) when herdr succeeded, else (None, why)."""
    try:
        done = call(["herdr"] + list(args), timeout)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return None, f"herdr {' '.join(args[:2])} timed out after {timeout} s"
    except OSError as e:
        return None, f"could not run herdr: {e}"
    # herdr prints a result on stdout, and an error as JSON on stderr.
    raw = done.stdout if (done.stdout or "").strip() else (done.stderr or "")
    try:
        reply = json.loads(raw)
    except ValueError:
        reply = None
    if done.returncode == 0:
        result = reply.get("result") if isinstance(reply, dict) else None
        return (result if isinstance(result, dict) else {}), None
    try:
        detail = reply["error"]["code"]
    except (TypeError, KeyError):
        detail = raw.strip()[:200]
    return None, f"herdr {' '.join(args[:2])} failed (exit {done.returncode}) {detail}".strip()


def read_state(path):
    """The switchboard's state file as {"watching": [...], "cycle": line or None}, or None."""
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            lines = [l.strip() for l in f.read().splitlines()]
    except OSError:
        return None
    watching, section = [], None
    for line in lines:
        if line.startswith("## "):
            section = line[3:].strip()
        elif section == "watching" and line and not line.startswith("#"):
            parts = line.split()
            if len(parts) >= 3:
                repo = os.path.expanduser(" ".join(parts[1:-1]))
                watching.append((parts[0], repo, parts[-1]))
    filled = [l for l in lines if l]
    cycle = filled[-1] if filled and filled[-1].startswith("CYCLE") else None
    return {"watching": watching, "cycle": cycle}


def find_switchboard(agents):
    for field in ("name", "title", "terminal_title_stripped"):
        for a in agents:
            if isinstance(a, dict) and a.get(field) == NAME:
                return a
    return None


def find_pane(agents, pane):
    for a in agents:
        if isinstance(a, dict) and pane in (a.get("pane_id"), a.get("name")):
            return a
    return None


def wait_status(repo, pane):
    """switchboard-wait --status lines for one repo, repo name dropped, or (None, why).

    Each line starts with the repo folder's name, which may hold spaces, so
    that whole name is taken off, not just the first word.

    The wait reads the same state file, so a CYCLE or DONE from before the run
    started is left out and never counts as this run's end.
    """
    try:
        done = call([child_python(), WAIT, "--status", "--state", STATE_FILE,
                     f"{repo}:{pane}"], HERDR_TIMEOUT + 15)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return None, f"switchboard-wait --status {repo}: {e}"
    if done.returncode != 0:
        return None, (f"switchboard-wait --status {repo} exit {done.returncode}: "
                      f"{(done.stderr or '').strip()[:200]}")
    name = os.path.basename(os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(repo))) + " "
    return [line[len(name):] for line in (done.stdout or "").splitlines()
            if line.startswith(name)], None


def load_json(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            d = json.load(f)
        return d if isinstance(d, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def save_json(path, d):
    tmp = f"{path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
        json.dump(d, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


class Pass:
    """One pass: what was seen, what was done, and the state carried to the next."""

    def __init__(self, state, dry, t, state_dir):
        self.state, self.dry, self.t, self.state_dir = state, dry, t, state_dir
        alerts = state.get("alerts")
        self.alerts = alerts if isinstance(alerts, dict) else {}
        self.can_prompt = False  # the switchboard is idle and nothing has gone to it yet
        self.switch_off = False
        self.seen = set()
        self.record = {"time": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z", time.localtime(t)),
                       "switchboard": None, "observed": [], "actions": [], "cleared": [],
                       "notes": [], "errors": []}

    def observe(self, repo, pane, condition):
        """The alert for this fingerprint, its pass count raised by one."""
        key = f"{repo}|{pane}|{condition}"
        old = self.alerts.get(key)
        a = old if isinstance(old, dict) else {"first": self.t, "count": 0}
        a["count"] = a.get("count", 0) + 1
        self.alerts[key] = a
        self.seen.add(key)
        self.record["observed"].append({"repo": repo, "pane": pane, "condition": condition,
                                        "count": a["count"]})
        a["key"] = key
        return a

    def keep(self, repo=None):
        """Carry alerts over unchanged when a pass could not look at them."""
        for key in self.alerts:
            if repo is None or key.startswith(f"{repo}|"):
                self.seen.add(key)

    def act(self, **action):
        self.record["actions"].append(action)
        if self.dry and action.get("ok") is None and action.get("dry_run"):
            what = action["kind"]
            if what == "banner":
                print(f"would banner: {action['text']}")
            elif what == "restart":
                print(f"would restart the switchboard in {legwork_dir()}")
            else:
                for text in action.get("texts") or [action["text"]]:
                    print(f"would prompt {action['to']}: {text}")

    def prompt(self, a, to, text):
        if a.get("prompt"):
            return
        base = {"kind": "prompt", "fingerprint": a["key"], "to": to, "text": text}
        if not self.can_prompt:
            self.act(ok=None, note="switchboard not idle or already prompted this pass, "
                                   "sent on a later pass", **base)
        elif self.dry:
            self.act(ok=None, dry_run=True, **base)
            self.can_prompt = False
        else:
            err = send(to, [text])
            a["prompt"] = err is None
            self.can_prompt = err is not None
            self.act(ok=err is None, error=err, **base)

    def banner(self, a, text):
        if a.get("banner"):
            return
        base = {"kind": "banner", "fingerprint": a["key"], "text": text}
        if self.dry:
            self.act(ok=None, dry_run=True, **base)
            return
        err = notify(text)
        if err:
            print(f"switchboard-health: no banner: {err}", file=sys.stderr)
        a["banner"] = err is None
        self.act(ok=err is None, error=err, **base)

    def save(self):
        os.makedirs(self.state_dir, exist_ok=True)
        save_json(os.path.join(self.state_dir, "health-state.json"), self.state)

    def finish(self, state_dir):
        alerts = {}
        for key, a in self.alerts.items():
            if key in self.seen:
                a.pop("key", None)
                alerts[key] = a
            else:
                self.record["cleared"].append(key)
        self.state["alerts"] = alerts
        self.state["last_pass"] = self.t
        line = json.dumps(self.record, sort_keys=True)
        if self.dry:
            print(line)
            if self.switch_off:
                print("would switch the health watcher off: "
                      + ("a new sign-in" if self.record.get("new_login") else "nothing to watch"))
            return
        self.save()
        with open(os.path.join(state_dir, "health.jsonl"), "a", encoding="utf-8",
                  newline="\n") as f:
            f.write(line + "\n")
        if self.switch_off:
            # Last, because under launchd this ends the pass's own process.
            try:
                call([child_python(), CTL, "off"], 60)
            except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
                print(f"switchboard-health: could not switch off: {e}", file=sys.stderr)


def count_off(p, sb):
    """Count passes with nothing to watch; the second in a row switches the watcher off."""
    if sb is None or (not sb["watching"] and not sb["cycle"]):
        n = p.state.get("off_count")
        n = (n if isinstance(n, int) else 0) + 1
    else:
        n = 0
    if n >= OFF_PASSES:
        p.switch_off = True
        p.act(kind="self-off")
        n = 0
    p.state["off_count"] = n


def send(pane, texts):
    """Send prompts in order, letting the agent settle between them. None or why not."""
    for i, text in enumerate(texts):
        if i:
            # Best effort: a slash command may never show as working.
            herdr("agent", "wait", pane, "--timeout", str(HERDR_TIMEOUT * 1000),
                  timeout=HERDR_TIMEOUT + 5)
        _, err = herdr("agent", "prompt", pane, text)
        if err:
            return err
    return None


def session_of(pane):
    """(herdr's session id for the agent in pane, None), or (None, why not)."""
    result, err = herdr("agent", "get", pane)
    if err:
        return None, err
    try:
        return result["agent"]["agent_session"]["value"], None
    except (KeyError, TypeError):
        return None, None


def cycle(pane):
    """Send the cycle prompts, the rest only once /clear has taken. None or why not."""
    before, err = session_of(pane)
    if err:
        return err
    if before is None:
        return "herdr shows no session id for the switchboard, so /clear cannot be confirmed"
    _, err = herdr("agent", "prompt", pane, CYCLE_PROMPTS[0])
    if err:
        return err
    # /clear starts a new Claude Code session, and herdr reports its new id.
    deadline = time.time() + CLEAR_TIMEOUT
    while True:
        after, _ = session_of(pane)
        if after is not None and after != before:
            break
        if time.time() >= deadline:
            return f"/clear did not start a new session within {CLEAR_TIMEOUT} s"
        time.sleep(CLEAR_POLL)
    # Best effort: if the new session lost herdr's name, the next pass still finds it.
    herdr("agent", "rename", pane, NAME)
    return send(pane, CYCLE_PROMPTS[1:])


def notify(text):
    """Show a banner. None when it was shown, else why not."""
    if WINDOWS:
        if not POWERSHELL:
            return "powershell.exe not found, so no Windows toast"
        script = base64.b64encode(TOAST.encode("utf-16-le")).decode("ascii")
        argv = [POWERSHELL, "-NoProfile", "-NonInteractive", "-ExecutionPolicy", "Bypass",
                "-EncodedCommand", script]
        env = dict(os.environ, LEGWORK_TOAST_TITLE=TITLE, LEGWORK_TOAST_TEXT=text)
        tool = "powershell.exe toast"
    else:
        if not NOTIFIER:
            return "terminal-notifier not found on PATH or in /opt/homebrew/bin"
        argv, env, tool = [NOTIFIER, "-title", TITLE, "-message", text], None, "terminal-notifier"
    try:
        done = call(argv, 30, env=env)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return f"{tool}: {e}"
    if done.returncode != 0:
        detail = plain_error((done.stderr or "") or (done.stdout or "")).strip()[:200]
        return f"{tool} exit {done.returncode} {detail}".strip()
    return None


def restart():
    """(ok, pane, error) for one attempt to bring the switchboard back."""
    env = []
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR"):
        env += ["--env", f"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR={os.environ['CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR']}"]
    # The new switchboard reads and writes the state file this pass reads.
    env += ["--env", f"LEGWORK_SWITCHBOARD_DIR={STATE_DIR}"]
    if os.environ.get("SWITCHBOARD_STATE"):
        env += ["--env", f"SWITCHBOARD_STATE={STATE_FILE}"]
    # An oh-my-zsh update question at shell start eats the first letter herdr
    # types, so `claude` arrives as `laude`. Elsewhere the variable does nothing.
    env += ["--env", "DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATE=true"]
    result, err = herdr("workspace", "create", "--cwd", legwork_dir(), "--label", NAME,
                        *env, "--no-focus")
    if err:
        return False, None, err
    try:
        pane = result["root_pane"]["pane_id"]
    except (KeyError, TypeError):
        pane = None
    if not valid_pane(pane):
        return False, None, f"herdr workspace create returned no usable root pane id: {pane!r}"
    _, err = herdr("pane", "rename", pane, NAME)
    if not err:
        _, err = herdr("agent", "start", NAME, "--kind", "claude", "--pane", pane,
                       "--timeout", str(START_TIMEOUT * 1000), "--", *session_args(),
                       timeout=START_TIMEOUT + 15)
    if not err:
        err = send(pane, RESUME_PROMPTS)
    return err is None, pane, err


def check_down(p):
    """Check 1 when the switchboard is missing: restart, or banner if that already failed."""
    a = p.observe("", "", "switchboard-down")
    last = p.state.get("last_restart")
    if isinstance(last, (int, float)) and p.t - last < RESTART_GAP:
        again = time.strftime("%H:%M", time.localtime(last + RESTART_GAP))
        p.banner(a, f"The switchboard is down and was restarted under an hour ago. "
                    f"No restart before {again}. {BY_HAND}")
        return
    if p.dry:
        p.act(kind="restart", ok=None, dry_run=True)
        return
    p.state["last_restart"] = p.t
    p.save()  # before the attempt, so a crash in it still holds the hourly cap
    ok, pane, err = restart()
    p.act(kind="restart", ok=ok, pane=pane, error=err)
    if err and "agent_not_ready" in err:
        p.banner(a, f"The switchboard restart stopped at agent_not_ready in pane {pane}. "
                    f"No retry this hour. {BY_HAND}")


def check_repo(p, agents, project, repo, pane, sw_idle, cycle, to, stalls):
    """Checks 3 and 4 for one watched repo."""
    lines, err = wait_status(repo, pane)
    if err:
        p.record["errors"].append(err)
        p.keep(repo)
        old = p.state.get("stalls", {}).get(f"{repo}|{pane}")
        if old:
            stalls[f"{repo}|{pane}"] = old
        return
    words = [l.split() for l in lines]
    if sw_idle and not cycle and ["wait", "none"] in words:
        a = p.observe(repo, "", "wait-none")
        if a["count"] >= 2:
            p.prompt(a, to, f"SWITCHBOARD HEALTH wait-none: {repo}")

    agent = find_pane(agents, pane)
    status = agent.get("agent_status") if agent else "gone"
    trailing = any(len(w) > 1 and w[0] not in ("pane", "wait") and w[1] in ("CYCLE", "DONE")
                   for w in words)
    condition = None
    if status == "blocked":
        condition = "pane blocked"
    elif status in READY and not trailing:
        condition = "pane idle with no CYCLE or DONE"
    if condition:
        a = p.observe(repo, pane, f"check-in:{condition}")
        if a["count"] >= 2:
            p.prompt(a, to, f"SWITCHBOARD HEALTH check-in {project}: {condition}")

    if status != "working":
        return
    try:
        mtime = os.path.getmtime(os.path.join(repo, ".legwork", "switchboard.md"))
    except OSError:
        mtime = None
    seq = agent.get("state_change_seq")
    key = f"{repo}|{pane}"
    old = p.state.get("stalls", {}).get(key)
    if isinstance(old, dict) and old.get("mtime") == mtime and old.get("seq") == seq:
        stalls[key] = old
        still = p.t - old.get("since", p.t)
        if still >= STALL:
            a = p.observe(repo, pane, "stall")
            minutes = int(still // 60)
            p.prompt(a, to, f"SWITCHBOARD HEALTH stall {project}: {minutes} min with no change")
            p.banner(a, f"{project}: pane {pane} working {minutes} min with no change "
                        "to its switchboard file or herdr state.")
    else:
        stalls[key] = {"mtime": mtime, "seq": seq, "since": p.t}


def check_cycle(p, marker, to, sw_idle):
    """Check 2: send the cycle, resend it once, then banner if it never takes."""
    a = p.observe("", to, f"cycle {marker[5:].strip()}")
    sends = a.get("sends", 0)
    base = {"kind": "cycle", "fingerprint": a["key"], "to": to,
            "texts": list(CYCLE_PROMPTS), "attempt": sends + 1}
    if not sw_idle:
        if not sends:
            p.act(ok=None, note="switchboard not idle, sent on a later pass", **base)
    elif sends < 2:
        if p.dry:
            p.act(ok=None, dry_run=True, **base)
            return
        a["sends"] = sends + 1
        err = cycle(to)
        p.act(ok=err is None, error=err, **base)
    else:
        p.banner(a, f"The switchboard did not cycle: {marker} is still the last line of "
                    f"its state file after two tries and pane {to} is idle. Send "
                    f"/switchboard resume there yourself.")


def run_pass(state_dir, dry, login=None):
    global STATE_FILE, STATE_DIR
    STATE_FILE, STATE_DIR = state_file(state_dir), state_dir
    p = Pass(load_json(os.path.join(state_dir, "health-state.json")), dry, now(), state_dir)
    current = login_mark() if login else None
    if current and current != login:
        p.record["notes"].append("a new sign-in since the watcher was switched on: "
                                 "switching it off, nothing checked")
        p.record["new_login"] = True
        p.switch_off = True
        p.act(kind="self-off")
        p.keep()
        p.finish(state_dir)
        return 0
    last = p.state.get("last_pass")
    if isinstance(last, (int, float)) and p.t - last > PASS_GAP:
        for a in p.alerts.values():
            if isinstance(a, dict):
                a["count"] = 0
        p.state["stalls"] = {}
        p.state["off_count"] = 0
        p.record["notes"].append(f"gap of {int((p.t - last) // 60)} min since the last pass: "
                                 "stall clocks and two-pass counts restarted")
    sb = read_state(STATE_FILE)
    count_off(p, sb)
    if sb is None:
        p.record["notes"].append(f"no state file at {STATE_FILE}: the switchboard has not run")
        p.keep()
        p.finish(state_dir)
        return 0
    result, err = herdr("agent", "list")
    agents = result.get("agents") if result else None
    if err or not isinstance(agents, list):
        err = err or "herdr agent list gave no agents"
        p.record["errors"].append(err)
        p.keep()
        p.banner(p.observe("", "", "herdr-unreachable"),
                 f"herdr is not answering, so the switchboard cannot be checked: {err}")
        p.finish(state_dir)
        return 0

    sw = find_switchboard(agents)
    sw_idle = False
    to = None
    if sw is None and not sb["watching"]:
        p.record["notes"].append("switchboard missing but its state file watches nothing: "
                                 "not restarted")
    elif sw is None:
        check_down(p)
    else:
        to, status = sw.get("pane_id"), sw.get("agent_status")
        p.record["switchboard"] = {"pane": to, "status": status}
        if status == "blocked":
            p.banner(p.observe("", to, "switchboard-blocked"),
                     f"The switchboard is blocked on a prompt in pane {to}. It needs you.")
        sw_idle = p.can_prompt = status in READY
        if not valid_pane(to):
            p.record["errors"].append(f"switchboard pane id {to!r} is not usable: nothing sent")
            sw_idle = p.can_prompt = False
        elif sb["cycle"]:
            check_cycle(p, sb["cycle"], to, sw_idle)
            if sw_idle:
                # It is cycling, or stuck at its cycle: nothing else goes to it this pass.
                p.can_prompt = False

    stalls = {}
    for project, repo, pane in sb["watching"]:
        try:
            if not valid_pane(pane):
                raise ValueError(f"pane id {pane!r} in the state file is not usable")
            check_repo(p, agents, project, repo, pane, sw_idle, sb["cycle"], to, stalls)
        except Exception as e:  # one bad repo must not stop the pass
            p.record["errors"].append(f"check of {repo} failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
            p.keep(repo)
            old = p.state.get("stalls")
            for key, clock in (old.items() if isinstance(old, dict) else ()):
                if key.startswith(f"{repo}|"):
                    stalls[key] = clock
    p.state["stalls"] = stalls
    p.finish(state_dir)
    return 0


def main(argv):
    if "-h" in argv or "--help" in argv:
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return 0
    once, dry, state_dir, login, env, path = False, False, None, None, {}, []
    args = list(argv)
    while args:
        arg = args.pop(0)
        if arg == "--once":
            once = True
        elif arg == "--dry-run":
            dry = True
        elif arg == "--state-dir" and args:
            state_dir = args.pop(0)
        elif arg == "--login" and args:
            login = args.pop(0)
        elif arg == "--path" and args:
            path.append(args.pop(0))
        elif arg == "--env" and args and ENV_KEY.fullmatch(args[0].partition("=")[0]) \
                and "=" in args[0]:
            key, _, value = args.pop(0).partition("=")
            env[key] = value
        else:
            once = False
            break
    if not once:
        print(__doc__.strip(), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    os.environ.update(env)
    if path:
        os.environ["PATH"] = os.pathsep.join(path + [os.environ.get("PATH", "")]).rstrip(
            os.pathsep)
    state_dir = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(state_dir or default_state_dir()))
    log_to_files(state_dir)
    return run_pass(state_dir, dry, login)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
